{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 2"},"body":"Source reading supports the stated bounded navigation relation; this is agent-authored and unreviewed.\n\nInspected: Read full captured jet/Sobolev quotient, harmonic-extension, energy and DN-operator definitions and main theorem, plus audited nonuniqueness statement.","content_sha256":"sha256:a6019c61837a470cff0f1f811a1f3ce4d3c04bb34bba2a7f2fdc5ad2aba14a2c","fingerprint":"sha256:7d4717ccf09160f784278ebba06267a7ffe538f42f00d6f45f5f5b1e35f05c36","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Source reading supports the stated bounded navigation relation; this is agent-authored and unreviewed.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:646bf2f842e2a169865e984174b96b855e6a368deff70ec7e916cfafa4cf6557","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.ScalarConductivity.main_nonuniqueness"],"explanation":"The formal MainStatement supplies two bounded measurable scalar conductivities on the radius-three ball in R3, uniformly positive with common finite bounds, both one near the boundary and differing on a set of positive measure. They share one weak Dirichlet-to-Neumann operator defined by unique harmonic extensions and the energy pairing. These match all four clauses of the paper nonuniqueness theorem.","fingerprint":"sha256:de73990317aecf9966170107afc2413858b44838eda055fa9134c3e46c0c6cc0","limitations":"The formal trace space is realized as H1/H10 using closures of smooth jets; identifying it with the customary H1/2 boundary model is the standard representation bridge, not independently machine-verified by this reading. This is not the smooth